<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n88111" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προνωπής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>stooping forwards, with
				head inclined,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στείχει π.,</span> of one in deep grief,
				<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Alc.</u>
				186
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ἐστι καὶ ψυχορραγεῖ,</span>
			of one dying, ib.<i><span class="en">
				143
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. λαβεῖν</span> to take her
				<i>as she fell fainting forward,</i> of the ministers of the
			altar taking up lphigenia, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				234
			</span></i> (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			metaph., <i>inclined, ready,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄγαν π. ἐς τὸ λοιδορεῖν φέρῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Andr.</u>
					729
				</span></i>
			. (Cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νωπέομαι.</span>)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
